# SRG-APP-000176-WSR-000096  -  CAT II
# Only authenticated system administrators or the designated PKI Sponsor for
# the web server must have access to the web servers private key.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000176-WSR-000096
group:           V-206389
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000186
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk's encrypt_fields list determines which configuration settings,
                 including the certificate key passwords, are stored encrypted under
                 splunk.secret rather than as readable text, which is the product's control
                 over who can obtain the web server private key's password from the
                 configuration layer.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [general] encrypt_fields matches sslPassword

external:        File system ownership and permissions on the private key, on the conf
                 files that hold its password, and on splunk.secret, which are operating
                 system controls and carry most of this objective
external:        Role-to-capability assignments that permit reading stored secrets through
                 the REST layer (for example list_storage_passwords and admin_all_objects)
                 are enabled per role in authorize.conf and verified against the role and
                 user assignments, not from a single setting; the capability names listed
                 against server.conf [general] in the key inventory are authorize.conf role
                 capabilities
external:        Designation of the PKI Sponsor, which is procedural
external:        Not Applicable where the web server has no private key

citation:        SRG-APP-000176-WSR-000096 check text (Not Applicable where the web server
                 has no private key); server.conf.spec:547-560 (encrypt_fields,
                 comma-separated <conf-file>:<stanza-prefix>:<setting> entries, default
                 list includes "server: :sslKeysfilePassword" and "server: :sslPassword"),
                 web.conf.spec:93-99 (web.conf sslPassword), web.conf.spec:75-80
                 (privKeyPath); authorize.conf.spec:67-78 (capabilities such as
                 list_storage_passwords and admin_all_objects are enabled per role stanza
                 in authorize.conf, not in server.conf)
finding:         server.conf [general] encrypt_fields has been overridden without an
                 sslPassword entry, so the web server private key's password is stored
                 unencrypted in the configuration where any reader of the conf layer can
                 obtain it.
